# Patterns for files to include in `yadm encrypt` → gpg archive.
# Mae's current policy (ADR 004): use PER-MACHINE SSH keys instead of
# tracking encrypted keys here. Better blast radius — compromising one
# machine's GPG doesn't expose other machines' SSH access.
#
# If you later want to track anything here, uncomment a pattern, run
# `yadm encrypt`, then `yadm add .local/share/yadm/archive` + commit.
# Uses asymmetric encryption to key C8ABE62412652B9E (set in .config/yadm/config).
